WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.330
- I'm gonna be making the
ultimate vegan ice cream.

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.450
It's gonna be the best
vanilla vegan ice cream

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:05.283
you've ever had.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.513
Is this wrong?

00:00:08.513 --> 00:00:09.633
- This is very weird.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:10.793
- I don't know.

00:00:10.793 --> 00:00:12.530
- It tastes like when
you walk into Home Depot.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.780
(groaning)

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.521
- We wanna give the people what they want.

00:00:19.521 --> 00:00:21.771
(laughing)

00:00:34.063 --> 00:00:36.550
I'm gonna try these two methods
that I've been researching.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.090
So, the first one, I'm gonna
be using frozen bananas.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.200
We've got these bad boys frozen solid.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.393
Oh, okay, that just looks
like a weird, old finger.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.550
I was rushing.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.920
Okay, nobody wants this
in their ice cream.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.170
It's gonna reach out of
a closet and get you.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.490
While we're waiting for those to freeze,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.136
I'm gonna try my second method,
which is with coconut milk.

00:00:57.136 --> 00:00:57.969
Oh, yeah.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.513
I mean, don't provoke me.

00:01:02.593 --> 00:01:07.176
♪ You keep pushin me aside and I can't ♪

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.023
We're gonna get there, Vaughn, promise.

00:01:13.023 --> 00:01:15.083
Smooth, not a chunk in site.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.560
Okay, so we've got these frozen, peeled,

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.230
pre-peeled bananas that I made.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.273
Oh, yeah, love that sound.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.800
Oh, that's nice, actually.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.910
I'm gonna go freeze this,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.723
and then we can go check on
these two bad boys tomorrow.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.353
That's not ideal.

00:01:33.353 --> 00:01:34.820
That's not the sound you wanna hear.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:37.883
I can chew it.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:45.670
Tastes like a banana.

00:01:50.407 --> 00:01:52.500
Van Leeuwen's is really delicious,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.223
but do you think they would give us tips?

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:56.670
- Should we go to Van Leeuwen?

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.520
- Yeah, let's just do it.
- Alright.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.930
- Okay, so we called Van Leeuwen Ice Cream

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.090
and it turns out the
founder of the company,

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.323
Ben Van Leeuwen, is
gonna be working today.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.970
So, we're gonna go get some
tips and tricks from him.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.510
I cannot believe this is happening.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:10.343
- Epic.

00:02:10.343 --> 00:02:11.230
- Alright, here we go.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.063
Woo hoo!

00:02:12.063 --> 00:02:14.614
(upbeat music)

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:18.220
I need to make the ultimate
vanilla vegan ice cream.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.053
- Okay, cool.

00:02:19.053 --> 00:02:20.760
- Would you give me a tip on kind of

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.330
how to bring out the vanilla flavor,

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:26.623
but to not let the coconut overpower it?

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:27.463
- Oh, that's good.

00:02:27.463 --> 00:02:28.296
Mmm.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.790
So, we think the best way
to make vegan ice cream now

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.250
is using coconut cream, cashew milk,

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.973
cocoa butter, and coconut oil.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.040
So, each of those things
plays a different role

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:44.390
in creating a super luscious,
chewy, creamy vegan ice cream.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.240
It's a good meal.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.093
Other than the sugar,
it's completely healthy.

00:02:47.093 --> 00:02:48.970
- I was gonna ask you,
can my cat eat this?

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.020
Because sometimes she licks my ice cream.

00:02:52.375 --> 00:02:53.650
Today I'm feeling a lot more confident

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.821
because I got to talk to
Ben freakin' Van Leeuwen,

00:02:55.821 --> 00:02:57.380
and now I'm gonna show you

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.350
some of the things that I learned.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:01.100
So, the first thing we're
gonna do is take these cashews

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.130
that I soaked overnight and
we're gonna make cashew milk.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.803
So, I'm gonna try to
gracefully dump this in here.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:07.740
I don't know if that's
even humanly possible,

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.090
but oh, good god.
- You got it.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.393
- Honestly, not so bad.

00:03:11.881 --> 00:03:12.714
Oh, yeah.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.019
- [Vaughn] Oh, mama.

00:03:17.019 --> 00:03:17.852
- [Merle] Is that good?

00:03:17.852 --> 00:03:20.123
- Oh, wow, that looks so good.

00:03:20.653 --> 00:03:21.623
This is thick.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:22.640
How many Cs?

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:23.782
- I think it warrants three.

00:03:23.782 --> 00:03:24.615
- Cheers.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:28.600
- Okay, so now we're going
to put the coconut milk

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.513
in with the cashew milk.

00:03:32.397 --> 00:03:33.230
Two cups.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.110
Now it's time to sauce it up.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.750
I'm gonna make simple syrup.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.130
So, that's just some water and some sugar.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.683
Let's mix that baby up.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:46.643
Why?

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:47.723
Saying what?

00:03:51.566 --> 00:03:52.520
I don't wanna talk about it.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:53.500
It's finally melting.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.690
I am also melting.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:55.890
The cocoa butter, I'm pretty sure,

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:59.470
is gonna help it stay fairly
solid while the coconut oil

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:02.820
should give it that meltiness
that we want in an ice cream.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.110
We don't want it to be rock solid

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.493
like the coconut nightmare
we saw yesterday.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.040
Oh, now's the time where you can add

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.750
the flavor that you want,
now that you have the base.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.030
I'm gonna use actual vanilla bean

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:15.193
'cause we're fancy schmancy around here.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.280
So, now we're gonna take this
and we're going to chill it

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.653
for an hour or two.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.473
We were supposed to
freeze this for 24 hours.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:30.340
- Go put that (bleep) thing

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:31.680
in the freezer right now, Merle.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.513
- I'm sorry!

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:33.970
I'm sorry.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.610
Alright, I'm gonna get the compressor.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.100
We're gonna test out our first batch

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:40.013
of Van Leeuwen influenced ice cream.

00:04:40.163 --> 00:04:42.310
It's so creamy and delicious.
- Wow.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:43.893
- Oh, look at that.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.393
It said just to press start.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.600
Oh my God (clapping).

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.923
We might have actual hope here, guys.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.560
Oh my God, I think I actually
did something right today.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.200
Look at that, and we
haven't even frozen it yet.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.663
(groaning) Oh my God.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:57.773
- No, I got it.

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:58.893
Here we go.

00:05:00.042 --> 00:05:00.988
- [Both] Oh!

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:02.170
- Get outta there, you.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.343
Wow, I'm very impressed with us.

00:05:04.343 --> 00:05:05.860
- That is beautiful.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:06.943
Oh, mama.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:08.700
- No, that's really good.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.270
That's like milk.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.103
- Yay!

00:05:11.103 --> 00:05:12.460
So, now I'm gonna freeze this because,

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:13.293
I mean, we gotta eat it,

00:05:13.293 --> 00:05:16.010
and then tomorrow we're gonna
try to perfect the flavor.

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:17.440
I think we've got the consistency down,

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.660
but now we wanna get that
delicious vanilla flavoring

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:21.923
and try to lose the undertones of coconut.

00:05:28.499 --> 00:05:30.582
So, my plan is to kind of

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.680
balance the fats out a little bit more.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:33.957
I'm gonna use less coconut oil

00:05:33.957 --> 00:05:35.660
and I'm gonna use more cocoa butter

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.430
so it has less of a coconutty flavor.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:39.513
So, that's basically what
we're gonna be working with

00:05:39.513 --> 00:05:40.393
with this batch.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.307
Now I have that batch whipped up

00:05:44.307 --> 00:05:45.920
and I'm gonna let is churn for an hour.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.990
And in the meantime, I'm
gonna test another recipe.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.340
I'm just playing with the levels

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.690
of cashew milk and coconut milk.

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:54.860
So, we've got ice cream flyin'
all over the place right now

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:56.310
is basically what I'm saying.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:01.473
Here she is!

00:06:02.844 --> 00:06:03.761
- Oh, yeah.

00:06:06.195 --> 00:06:07.028
Hm.

00:06:07.028 --> 00:06:09.153
- It kinda has a bad breath aftertaste.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.353
- I don't love it.

00:06:10.353 --> 00:06:11.717
- Papery, wooden kinda thing.
(laughing)

00:06:11.717 --> 00:06:13.490
- The flavor's very odd.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:14.473
- What do we do?

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:16.530
I don't know what to do.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:17.630
- [Vaughn] Oh, wait, Claire!

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:18.463
- Claire, help us.
- Let's get Claire

00:06:18.463 --> 00:06:20.283
to taste this.
- Claire, please.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:21.940
Taste this and be mean,

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.340
but then be nice and tell
me the texture's good.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:32.630
- 'Cause I know you guys have been working

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:36.080
really hard on this,
but this is very weird.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.900
- So, okay, so what this is is...

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:40.630
- You need a lot more vanilla.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:41.633
- More vanilla?

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:42.493
- Yeah, one...

00:06:42.493 --> 00:06:43.630
I don't think one bean's that strong.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.110
I think that we can up the vanilla

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:47.020
just to kind of overpower that flavor.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:47.853
- I'm scared.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.250
Wood and Play-Doh.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:51.810
Okay, we have been asking for help

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.080
and people keep telling
us it doesn't taste good,

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.630
but nobody knows how to fix it.

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:56.640
I don't know what to do.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.880
I wanna keep testing
'cause it's already Friday

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.910
and we've been shooting this since Monday,

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:02.680
and also, we're running out of resources.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.490
And this isn't a Game of Thrones budget,

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.703
so we can't afford to keep buying stuff.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.000
Okay, no, I'm just frustrated because

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.700
I just want it to be
something that I'm proud of,

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.773
and I'm not proud of what we have so far.

00:07:16.856 --> 00:07:19.350
I'm getting so desperate I
almost feel like we should DM Ben

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:21.073
and just ask him for help.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.533
- Like Ben Van Leeuwen?
- Yeah, I don't know.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.574
- [Vaughn] DM him, you
should seriously DM him.

00:07:26.574 --> 00:07:28.623
- I feel like a maniac doing this.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:29.900
Hey, Ben, I'm so sorry to bother you,

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.630
but we're having an ice cream crisis.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.773
Oh my God, am I actually sending this?

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.123
- [Vaughn] Send.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.980
- Now I'm just gonna be
sitting here watching it.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.420
This is turning into a reality TV show.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.677
- [Vaughn] Whoa, look at that.

00:07:40.677 --> 00:07:41.510
(mumbling)

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:43.523
- Sorry, I'm so annoyed right now.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.800
It just tastes like wood and licorice.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:47.913
The texture's good,

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.183
and now I just wanna cry
because we're out of money

00:07:49.183 --> 00:07:50.819
and we're out of time and...

00:07:50.819 --> 00:07:52.410
- It's okay, Merle,
you're gonna make it work.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.243
So, there's cocoa butter in it?

00:07:53.243 --> 00:07:54.076
Can I taste it?

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.280
- Yeah, I actually
didn't even taste it yet.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.823
- Oh, that's a little weird.

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:02.100
You know, it's like...

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.960
It tastes like when you
walk into Home Depot

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.270
and you smell the weird wood in the air.

00:08:06.563 --> 00:08:07.396
- That is what it is.
- What?

00:08:07.396 --> 00:08:09.224
- It's so bad.
- It tastes like wood.

00:08:09.224 --> 00:08:10.757
- This is what it is.
- It smells like wood.

00:08:10.757 --> 00:08:11.590
- Wait.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:12.935
- That is the weird aftertaste.

00:08:12.935 --> 00:08:13.768
- Why didn't we taste this before?

00:08:13.768 --> 00:08:16.313
- Close your eyes and
walk into Home Depot.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.240
- Smack my fanny and call me Sally.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:19.210
That is what it is!

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:20.350
- Here's what I'm gonna do,

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:23.740
I'm gonna take it down from
six tablespoons of cocoa butter

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:26.190
to four and I'm gonna
bring up the coconut oil

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.783
from two tablespoons to four.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:32.453
We're gonna add in the coconut
milk and the cashew milk,

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.970
and then we're going to emulsify it.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:37.180
I'm going to actually start the blender

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.473
with these in it already,

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:42.380
and then I'm going to slowly
pour in the sugar water mixture

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:44.663
to make sure that they
really blend together.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:46.663
Woo, emulsify!

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:48.930
It sounds like a great spell.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:54.950
We'll be cutting around that.

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:00.963
I'm gonna go chill this,
and I'm gonna chill,

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.520
and then we're gonna churn
it and call it a day.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.353
We're almost done.

00:09:04.353 --> 00:09:06.100
- Knock on wood.
- Knock on

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.140
whatever you have nearby.

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:09.007
Oh, there's some wood.

00:09:09.097 --> 00:09:11.764
(country music)

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:16.210
- We don't wanna over churn it.

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.760
- Okay, I'm gonna churn it off.

00:09:18.638 --> 00:09:20.233
(laughing)

00:09:20.233 --> 00:09:22.333
Should we take a little teeny taste of it?

00:09:25.596 --> 00:09:27.513
That is so much better.

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:29.303
- [Vaughn] No, really?

00:09:29.303 --> 00:09:30.820
- You're about to scream to the heavens.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:31.969
- Oh my god.
- I know!

00:09:31.969 --> 00:09:32.999
It's so much better!

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:35.630
- My god, wait, that's so good!

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.430
- [Merle] I think we've figured it out.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.173
- [Vaughn] Oh my God.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.420
- I'm so happy right now.

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:42.170
- [Vaughn] This feels like victory.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:43.703
- Oh, mama.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:45.093
Whoa, we are done.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:46.490
I'm ready to wrap this puppy up.

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:47.560
Let's get some people in here to try it.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.120
This is a very important taste tester

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:50.536
because Rachel's vegan.

00:09:50.536 --> 00:09:53.336
- This is gonna be some Gordon
Ramsey review right here.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.130
- The eye contact is everything.

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:56.663
No pressure.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.173
- Holy (bleep).

00:09:59.364 --> 00:10:00.315
- It's (bleep) delicious.

00:10:00.315 --> 00:10:01.148
- [Merle] Yes!

00:10:01.148 --> 00:10:02.203
- I am so impressed.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:05.700
- Yeah, this is nice, this is good.

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:08.990
- This struggle was so real.

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:11.097
Easily the hardest Tasty
video I've ever made,

00:10:11.097 --> 00:10:13.150
and certainly the longest.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:15.970
I don't know if I could've
done it without you, for sure.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:17.150
I think I probably would've given up.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.123
- Oh, stop it.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:19.820
Let's eat some of that ice cream.

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:20.700
It's really good.
- I mean,

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.498
we have like 19 tubs of ice cream now.

00:10:22.498 --> 00:10:24.733
Woo, let's go see Mama
Mia Two, not a plug.

00:10:27.861 --> 00:10:30.444
(upbeat music)

